#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:45
msgid "A challenge interrupts the race until its participants finish. Some challenges are only for two players; the others can also be drawn for a group. In simultaneous challenges, your answers and attempts stay hidden until the result is revealed. In turn-based challenges, each move is public."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:45
msgid "A challenge interrupts the race until its participants finish. Some challenges are only for two players; the others can also be drawn for a group. Your answers and individual attempts stay hidden until the result is revealed, except in games where players take turns, such as numbered balls and sound pairs."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:45
msgid "A challenge interrupts the race until its result is decided. Some challenges are only for two players; the others can also be drawn for a group. In simultaneous challenges, your answers and attempts stay hidden until the result is revealed. In turn-based challenges, each move is public."
