msgid "No limit, the default, allows any legal raise up to your stack. Pot limit allows a raise above the call up to the pot after adding that call. Half-pot limit uses half of that amount, but never sets the ceiling below a minimum legal raise. Your remaining stack is still the final limit. Fixed limit uses a raise equal to the current big blind throughout the hand. Unlike some poker rules, our fixed-limit amount does not double in later betting rounds."
